Our free communities are for anyone living with a long-term health condition or disability, and for the people who care for them. Join one, or both.

{% community /%}

## What you will find

- **People who get it.** Share good days and bad days with others living with similar conditions.
- **Help with benefits.** Ask questions about PIP, DLA, Attendance Allowance and ADP, and hear what helped other people.
- **Condition chats.** Our Discord has chats for more than 50 health conditions, and a live voice chat when you want to talk.

## Keeping everyone safe

Both communities have simple rules that everyone agrees to when they join. In short:

- be kind, and respect that everyone is on their own journey
- keep personal details private, including National Insurance and benefit reference numbers
- what is shared in the community stays in the community
- posts are personal experiences, not medical, legal or financial advice

For advice about your own situation, speak to your GP, a pharmacist or a free adviser such as Citizens Advice.

{% callout type="danger" title="If you need help now" %}
If you or someone else is in danger, call **999**. You can talk to **Samaritans** free, day or night, on **116 123**. See [more places to get help](/get-help-now/).
{% /callout %}

## Your privacy

Our groups run on Facebook and Discord, so their own privacy policies apply, and other members can see what you post. Read how we handle information in our [privacy policy](/privacy-policy/).
